  'how.source': 'Source',
  'how.chat.1': 'A turn runs these stages in order: ensure, compaction (skipped: the Lab never compacts), reindex, recall, prompt, stream, persist, flush_decision, flush.',
  'how.chat.2': 'The flush decision comes after the reply (upstream v2026.9.6 session maintenance, no prompt estimate). When triggered, the flush turn gets the Project Context and may only append to today\'s daily file; its reply is never shown. /flush forces one run (Lab extension).',
  'how.chat.3': 'Auto-recall is demo-only: memory_search runs on the user message; only MEMORY.md and today\'s/yesterday\'s daily file reach the prompt. Off for subagent/cron and reset turns.',
  'how.chat.4': 'The transcript window is demo-only: last 40 messages, 24,000 chars.',
  'how.chat.5': 'The tool loop is the Lab\'s (host): memory_search, memory_get (upstream definitions) and the curation tools; at most 6 tool rounds plus 1 final round without tools. Curated writes are an extension with per-target flags.',
  'how.chat.6': 'Without a key the chat answers 400 no_api_key; there is no fake model.',
  'how.chat.7': '/new and /reset run the host kit\'s session-memory hook (memory/<date>-<HHMM>.md, raw lines, no redactor, D2), index the file at once and start a new session: same key (lab:<kind>, upstream sessionKey), new id; a pending bootstrap completes before a bare command sends the reset prompt in its own turn.',
  'how.chat.src': 'docs/lab.md › A chat turn · What is real, what is not',
  'how.heartbeat.1': 'Runtime-only port: the host owns the scheduler; in the Lab the heartbeat runs by hand. {project} computes the due automation jobs and the prompt.',
  'how.heartbeat.2': 'Instructions live in the monitor scratch (HEARTBEAT.md is never read): empty scratch is skipped (empty-heartbeat-file), no scratch runs the generic prompt, due jobs always run.',
  'how.heartbeat.3': 'A run streams either a skip (skipped) or the prompt, tool calls, the reply and the decision, then the flush decision (runtime_skip:heartbeat: heartbeats never flush). Jobs that ran get their next due time.',
  'how.heartbeat.4': 'Reply decision (/heartbeat/reply): NO_REPLY and a legacy HEARTBEAT_OK ack (300-character rule) are not delivered; a trailing notify=false line delivers silently.',
  'how.heartbeat.src': 'docs/lab.md › What is real, what is not · Endpoints',
  'how.consolidation.1': 'Curated writes are an extension: MemoryCurator, per-target flags and the master flag curated_memory_writes.',
  'how.consolidation.2': 'Promotion and dreaming are package code; sweeps run by hand. The view\'s evidence label is read from docs/parity_matrix.md.',
  'how.consolidation.3': 'The short-term recall store counts how often, with which queries and with which score a line was recalled.',
  'how.consolidation.4': 'Dreaming phases: light revisits the candidates and records signals; REM appends a trace to DREAMS.md; deep moves the candidates that pass the gates into MEMORY.md.',
  'how.consolidation.5': 'Phase signals give candidates extra weight; on their own they never bypass promotion.',
  'how.consolidation.src': 'docs/lab.md › What is real, what is not · docs/parity_matrix.md',
  'how.live.1': 'Adapter-only: LiveTaskDemo runs over {projectPackage}.live in its own workspace ($TMPDIR/{projectName}-live-task-demo-workspace).',
  'how.live.2': 'A real model when a request or .env key resolves, else scripted replies.',
  'how.live.3': 'Summaries redact the identity proof.',
  'how.live.4': 'SDK events are mirrored to the bus as live.<type> (Timeline tab).',
  'how.live.src': 'docs/lab.md › What is real, what is not · Kept /api/*',
  'parity.how.1': 'The results file is built by demo/parity_results.py from the JUnit output of the oracle and memory-tools tests.',
  'parity.how.2': 'Each test\'s evidence kind is classified statically from the test source: python_eq_ts (oracle and {project} in the same test), ts_literal (oracle only, Python two-hop), python_eq_source (Python constants against the upstream source text), python_literal (no oracle).',
  'parity.how.3': 'Matrix rows are read from docs/parity_matrix.md. A row may say match only when an executable oracle operation compares Python behavior against the pinned OpenClaw TypeScript checkout.',
  'parity.how.4': 'The parity trace (/api/parity/trace) has 5 steps: the promotion/dreaming chain only.',
  'parity.how.src': 'docs/lab.md › Parity results · docs/parity_matrix.md',
  'how.memory.1': 'memory_search takes query, maxResults, minScore and corpus (all|memory|sessions|wiki); invalid input answers 400 tool_input_error with the verbatim upstream message.',
  'how.memory.2': 'Each search runs with a 15 s deadline; a timeout or error starts a 60 s cooldown, during which memory is not searched.',
  'how.memory.3': 'Embeddings: a real endpoint gives hybrid search; otherwise FTS-only and no embedder is built. Never fake vectors.',
  'how.memory.4': 'The this-turn section shows the demo-only auto-recall: only MEMORY.md and today\'s/yesterday\'s daily file reach the prompt.',
  'how.memory.src': 'docs/memory_search_tool.md › Deadline and cooldown · docs/lab.md',
